# Atomic Design and component-first UI

Do not dump a screen into a route file. Build and reuse components, then compose them into templates and pages. Prefer `@mantine/core` when a component exists. Colocate a `.module.css` only when layout still needs it.

Atomic Design is not a waterfall. Zoom into a component, then step back to the page.

## Layers

| Layer | Owns | Does not own |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Atom | One HTML control or styled wrapper | Other app components, data fetching, page layout |
| Molecule | A small group of atoms with one job | Section-level layout, route data |
| Organism | A distinct section: header, plant list | Route loaders, URL params |
| Template | Page skeleton and slots | Fetching, domain records, real copy |
| Page | Route module: call query hooks, wire a template | New atoms invented inline |

When unsure, go **one level lower** and compose up.

## Folder tree

Reusable UI lives under `apps/web/app/components/`. Route modules stay pages.

```
apps/web/app/
  components/
    atoms/
    molecules/
    organisms/
    templates/
  queries/
    hooks/
  routes/
    gardens.tsx
    my-garden.tsx
  root.tsx
  routes.tsx
```

One component per folder, named after the component (`SearchField`, not `HomeSearch`). `root.tsx` is the HTML document. `routes.tsx` only registers routes.

## Dependency direction

```
pages → templates → organisms → molecules → atoms
```

- Lower layers never import higher layers. Atoms never import other app components.
- Pages call hooks in `app/queries/hooks/`. Never `useQuery`/`useMutation` or `fetch` in routes, atoms, molecules, or templates.
- Do not import another component's `.module.css`.

## Component-first workflow

1. Inventory the UI pieces before writing a route.
2. Reuse `@mantine/core`, then `app/components/`. Do not invent Button, Title, Text, Stack, or TextInput atoms.
3. Place each new piece at the lowest honest layer.
4. Build atoms → molecules → organisms → template, then wire the page.
5. Verify the page in the browser for visual work.

## Agent do / don't

**Do**

- Search `@mantine/core` and existing components before creating new ones
- Keep route modules thin: call query hooks, pass props, render a template
- Extract a molecule when the same atom cluster appears twice

**Don't**

- Implement a feature as one large JSX tree in a route module
- Put `useQuery` / `useMutation` in routes, atoms, molecules, or templates
- Import a molecule from an atom, or a page from a template

## Good / bad

```tsx
// Bad — monolithic route; new atoms inline; fetch in the component
export default function HomePage() {
  const [gardens, setGardens] = useState([]);

  useEffect(() => {
    fetch('/gardens').then((r) => r.json()).then(setGardens);
  }, []);

  return (
    <div>
      <header>
        <form>
          <input />
          <button type="submit">Go</button>
        </form>
      </header>
      <ul>
        {gardens.map((g) => (
          <li key={g.id} style={{ padding: 12 }}>
            {g.name}
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  );
}
```
